title: config get --json wraps scalar values but not ref values
updated: 2026-08-12T00:02:49Z
---

karr config get KEY --json is inconsistent about wrapping:

    $ karr config get claim_timeout --json
    {"claim_timeout":"1h"}          # wrapped in its key

    $ karr config get board --json
    {"name":"App::karr"}            # the bare value, NOT wrapped

    $ karr config get statuses --json
    ["backlog",...]                 # bare too

So a consumer cannot tell a wrapped scalar from a bare mapping: the board
answer looks exactly like the wrapped form and is not one. Reading it as
{"board": ...} silently yields the wrong shape, and there is no key in the
payload to disambiguate.

Found while fixing #130, deliberately left alone there: unifying this is a
break in a machine-readable interface with no actual bug behind it, so it
wants its own decision rather than a drive-by change. Options are to wrap
consistently (breaks anyone reading list/mapping keys today) or to never
wrap (breaks anyone reading scalar keys today). t/49 and t/64 pin the
current behaviour for ref values.
